# Menu System Rules (Header & Mega Menu)

Port reference: `wp-content/themes/shineon/src/sass/menu/`  
Implementation plan: `context/plans/header-mega-menu-plan.md`

## Goals

1. **Self-contained menu token layer** — menu Sass reads global theme tokens but does not hard-wire `theme.json` CSS variables inside component partials.
2. **Single breakpoint control** — one variable + mixins decide desktop nav vs mobile drawer.
3. **Keyboard-safe styling** — focus states paired with hover; open states driven by ARIA/JS, not hover alone.

---

## Directory structure

Menu styles live in **`src/sass/menu/`**. Header shell (announcement, search row, utilities) stays in **`src/sass/header/`**.

```
src/sass/menu/
├── _index.scss                 # Entry — import order matters
├── _variables.scss             # Menu semantic tokens (maps from global settings)
├── _mixins.scss                # Menu breakpoint + panel + a11y mixins
├── _structure.scss             # Shared layout (lists, panels, z-index)
├── _desktop.scss               # Desktop nav row + mega panels
├── _mobile-drawer.scss         # #chairforce-mobile-drawer, drill-down
├── _labels.scss                # site-header__menu-label desktop/mobile toggle
├── _link-types/
│   ├── _index.scss
│   ├── _default.scss
│   ├── _heading.scss
│   ├── _thumbnail-link.scss    # 54×54 display, chairforce-menu-thumb
│   ├── _highlight-link.scss
│   └── _utility-link.scss
├── _layout-patterns/           # Figma patterns A / B / C
│   ├── _grouped-text.scss
│   ├── _flat-grid.scss
│   └── _grouped-thumbnails.scss
└── _animations.scss            # Mega panel open (port megaMenuAnimation logic)
```

Import in main `src/sass/index.scss`:

```scss
@import "header";   // shell only
@import "menu";    // nav + mega menu + drawer
```

**Do not** put mega menu rules in global `_mixins.scss` except re-exports if needed. Menu-specific mixins belong in `menu/_mixins.scss`.

---

## Variable layering (three tiers)

### Tier 1 — Global (existing)

- `src/sass/_settings.scss` — `$breakpoints`, header heights, spacing
- `src/sass/_theme-json-variable.scss` — theme.json → Sass colour/type tokens

### Tier 2 — Menu semantic (`menu/_variables.scss`)

Define **menu-only** variables that **reference** Tier 1 — never duplicate raw hex/px from Figma here without mapping through globals:

```scss
// Breakpoint key — single place to change mobile/desktop switch
$menu-breakpoint-key: navigation; // → 767px in _settings.scss

// Mega menu
$menu-mega-panel-bg: $color-background;
$menu-mega-heading-color: $color-neutral;
$menu-thumb-display-size: 54px;

// Mobile drawer
$menu-drawer-bg: $color-background;
$menu-drawer-bar-height: 3rem;
```

Component partials use **`$menu-*`** and **`$color-*`** from Tier 1/2 — **not** `var(--wp--preset--*)` directly.

### Tier 3 — Component partials

`_desktop.scss`, `_link-types/*`, etc. consume Tier 2 only.

---

## Breakpoint mixins (single control point)

Define in **`menu/_mixins.scss`**. All menu desktop/mobile splits **must** use these — never raw `@media` or global `@include breakpoint(navigation)` inside menu partials.

**Chairforce uses `$breakpoints.navigation` (767px)** — not shineon's `large` (1024px).

```scss
@mixin breakpoint-menu-up {
  @media screen and (min-width: #{map-get($breakpoints, $menu-breakpoint-key)}) {
    @content;
  }
}

@mixin breakpoint-menu-down {
  @media screen and (max-width: #{map-get($breakpoints, $menu-breakpoint-key)}) {
    @content;
  }
}

// Readable aliases — use when intent matters
@mixin menu-desktop-only {
  @include breakpoint-menu-up { @content; }
}

@mixin menu-mobile-only {
  @include breakpoint-menu-down { @content; }
}
```

To change when the menu becomes mobile: update **`$menu-breakpoint-key`** in `_variables.scss` (and `_settings.scss` `$breakpoints.navigation` if the pixel value changes).

### Other menu mixins (port/adapt from shineon)

Keep in `menu/_mixins.scss`:

| Mixin | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `site-header-menu` | Scope block: `.site-header { @content }` |
| `menu-mega-panel-hidden` / `menu-mega-panel-visible` | Closed/open panel visibility |
| `menu-drawer-min-height` | Drawer min-height minus header (port `mobileMenuMinimumHeight`) |
| `menu-link-with-icon` | Flex row for icon + label |
| `menu-interactive-states` | Shared `:hover` + `:focus-visible` block |

