## Selector scope & naming

All menu Sass scopes under **`.site-header`**. See plan § Naming conventions:

- Menu locations: `chairforce-primary-nav`, `chairforce-utility-nav` (PHP constants)
- Classes: `.site-header__mega-menu`, `.site-header__mobile-drawer`, `.site-header__nav-item--align-right`
- **Never** bare `.mobile-menu`, `.mega-menu`, `#mobile-menu` (Woodmart collision)

Walker may output WordPress `.menu-item` classes — style via `.site-header .menu-item`, not global `.menu-item` alone.

---

## Interaction & accessibility (CSS)

**Plan decision:** mega panels open on **click/tap** (JS sets `aria-expanded`, `.is-open`). CSS must not rely on `:hover` alone.

### Open / active states (desktop mega menu)

Style open panels using **all** of:

```scss
.site-header__nav-item--has-mega {
  &.is-open,
  &[aria-expanded='true'] {
    // trigger styling
  }

  &.is-open .site-header__mega-menu,
  &[aria-expanded='true'] .site-header__mega-menu {
    // panel visible
  }

  // Keyboard: keep panel accessible while focus inside
  &:focus-within .site-header__mega-menu {
    // match open panel styles when tabbing through
  }
}
```

`:hover` may **supplement** desktop styling but must **not** be the only selector that reveals content or indicates state.

### Links and buttons

Always pair hover with keyboard focus:

```scss
// ✅ Good
.site-header__nav-link {
  &:hover,
  &:focus-visible {
    color: $color-primary;
  }
}

// ❌ Bad — hover only
.site-header__nav-link:hover { ... }

// ❌ Bad — outline removed without replacement
outline: none;
```

Prefer **`:focus-visible`** over bare `:focus` for mouse users (avoid focus ring on click when possible). Buttons/triggers must keep a visible focus indicator.

### Mobile drawer

- Open: `html.menu-open` or `[aria-hidden='false']` on `#chairforce-mobile-drawer`
- Focus trap is JS; CSS supports `:focus-visible` on drawer links and visible focus on close/back buttons
- Body scroll lock: `html.menu-open { overflow: hidden; }` inside `@include menu-mobile-only`

### Label visibility

Desktop/mobile labels: CSS toggle inside `@include breakpoint-menu-up` / `@include menu-mobile-only` on `.site-header__menu-label--desktop` / `--mobile` — not `wp_is_mobile()`.

